{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"e47e (pip-audit unblock): Gerrit change 1239 pushed; pip-audit job PASSES in CI (run 30772193145), proving the fix. Root cause: inspect-ai (via [eval] extra) caps click!=8.2.0,<8.2.2,>=8.1.3, so uv universal resolution pinned click to the vulnerable 8.2.1. The uv version was NOT the cause; uv lock --upgrade-package click was a no-op because it only permits movement inside the existing constraint set. constraint-dependencies CANNOT fix this (it only narrows); override-dependencies is the right instrument. Fix = [tool.uv] override-dependencies = [click>=8.3.3] + relock -> click 8.4.2. inspect-ai cap is stale not real: 0.3.251 imports and runs its CLI under click 8.4.2; upstream PR UKGovernmentBEIS/inspect_ai#4596 relaxes it. Verified: uv lock --check passes under uv 0.7.18 AND 0.12.1 (lock stays revision 2), uv sync --locked --extra dev resolves, pip-audit --desc clean over whole env, 1463 tests pass. Follow-up 9fb3 filed for the untested [eval]/inspect-ai path."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785713287024587001,"uuid":"25c47f58-dcc6-4639-84db-b988919f4a67"}